  "worked_solution": "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $6$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n6=\\frac{6}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{2}{5}$ is $\\frac{5}{2}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n6÷\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{6}{1}÷\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. Note that we can simplify the process by swapping the denominators first.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{2} & =\\frac{6}{2}\\times \\frac{5}{1} \\\\  & =3\\times 5 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$",
